From caeb4f2d96766a52eefdc60542a646bd7985d04d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Latorrey Whitehead <torreyw94@tsmatter.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:41:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(digital-twin): correct inverted LIVE/SAMPLE label + add
 honest per-panel data badges

- hydrateAndRender() had the live-data condition inverted: it displayed
  'LIVE DATA' precisely when NO upload existed (i.e. on the hardcoded/
  drifting sample domain scores), and never showed a SAMPLE label at
  all. Fixed the condition and renamed usingLiveData -> usingLiveDomains
  for clarity, matching usingLiveSignals/usingLiveForecasts.
- These live-status flags are now reset at the top of every
  hydrateAndRender() pass instead of only being set on success, so a
  removed/failed upload correctly falls back to an honest SAMPLE label
  instead of keeping a stale LIVE one.
- Added domainMeta/forecastMeta badge spans (matching the existing
  signalMeta pattern) so DOMAIN HEALTH and 30-DAY FORECAST panels each
  show their own LIVE (UPLOADED) vs SAMPLE DATA status at the component
  level, not just in the LIVE DATA upload widget's label text.
- DOMAINS/FORECASTS still ship with placeholder demo numbers (same as
  every other vertical's LOAD SAMPLE DATA button) but are now honestly
  labeled instead of falsely claiming to be live.
---
 html/war-rooms/digital-twin/digital-twin.html | 48 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

